    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes! I used an AI tutor (like Wolfram Alpha or Khan Academy’s tools) for algebraic proofs. It helped visualize steps without overwhelming me with jargon. The low extraversion score (31) made interactive tools feel less intimidating than lectures, but only when the responses were clear and tailored. It saved time on repetitive drills and forced me to think differently.",
